  "confidence": 0.95,
  "rationale": "The RBI directions mandate that the periodic review of risk categorisation of accounts must be done at least once every six months, whereas the bank's policy limits this review only to the time of periodic updation of KYC (which occurs every 2, 8, or 10 years depending on the risk category), thereby creating a conflict due to a weaker timeline."
